ttps:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/microphones\/","url_meta":{"origin":25,"position":1},"title":"Microphones","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"To explain how I approach the discussed subject, we\u2019ll start at the audio source, the drum set. Traditional drum microphones have a certain amount of leakage from their surroundings, for example a mic placed to record the snare would also record quite an amount of hi-hat. I want to be\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"ukko","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/3.jpg?fit=1024%2C683&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":85,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/23\/equipment-standard-microphones-triggering\/","url_meta":{"origin":25,"position":2},"title":"Equipment standard (Microphones &#8211; triggering)","date":"September 23, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"Lydrommet were also kind enough to lend me some microphones. I tested them with the same intent as I tested the preamps, I wanted to see if there was any reason for me to invest in other microphones. I already have this one in all my drums: Also I have\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/10-4.jpg?fit=494%2C1200&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":362,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/25\/project-description\/","url_meta":{"origin":25,"position":3},"title":"Project description","date":"October 25, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"Project description: Performance with realtime interaction between drums and electronics. Goal: To develop a setup with drums and electronics which shall be practical and easy to operate. Why I do this: Amongst guitarists and some what keyboard players, the integration of audio processing and the interaction between the instrument and\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"","width":0,"height":0},"classes":[]},{"id":31,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/processing\/","url_meta":{"origin":25,"position":4},"title":"Processing","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"The total signal latency, in+out, in the signal-flow is at around 8ms. This presents a challenge regarding timing and I had to choose the effects I use based some what on this. I did a quick run-through of available effects in Ableton Live and Max for Live and checked how\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"space echo","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/5.jpg?fit=718%2C295&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":14,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/why\/","url_meta":{"origin":25,"position":5},"title":"Why?","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"So, why am I doing this? I\u2019ve always been jealous at the guitarists ability to just go and buy an effect pedal, send the sound of his guitar trough it and control it with his feet. I want to do the same thing, just that my instrument is a drum\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.files.wordpress.com\/2011\/09\/2.jpg?w=350&h=200&crop=1","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]}],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/25"}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=25"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"